ganized (reliability). No info on stress resilience, communication, responsibility. Mixed.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Concerns: can be grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). No info on decision speed, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (crew cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (crew cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strong on reliability and decision, weak on communication and adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew cooperation), relatively weak leadership (crew cooperation). No info on reliability, stress resilience maybe okay, decision quality unknown.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Candidate C seems strong on reliability and decision, but communication issues could be serious for cockpit. Candidate B strong on stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate D strong on problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership. Candidate A strong on anticipation and leadership but unorganized.\n\nProbably Candidate C is the strongest overall despite communication issues, but we need to discuss. As first contribution, we can propose Candidate C, acknowledging strengths and concerns, and ask others for more info on communication and adaptability.\n\nWe should reference facts: reliability 100%, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWe can say we currently recommend Candidate C, but we need to verify communication concerns.\n\nThus produce public message with vote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
